# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is a per machine setting, so a Windows clone rewrites every
# text file to CRLF on checkout unless a rule here says otherwise. A shell
# script cannot survive that. `set -euo pipefail` becomes `set -euo pipefail\r`,
# and the shell rejects an option named "pipefail\r" rather than running the
# script, which is how demo.sh stopped working from anything but Git Bash.
#
# The committed blobs were always LF. This file makes the working tree agree
# with them, on every machine, whatever core.autocrlf says locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary. Never touched, never diffed as text.
*.parquet binary
*.duckdb  binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.zip     binary
